  "body": "## What changed\n\nFound on the contributor's real Tormach 770MX during #521's hands-on probe test. Two things alarmed the operator: a new Probe op searched **5 mm** past the expected face (`G38.2 Z-0.1969`), and its approach was a **rapid straight down** to 0.197 in over the part.\n\n- **Shorter default search:** a new Probe op's probe distance is `default_overtravel(tolerance) = max(2 × tolerance, 1 mm)`, which is 1 mm for the seeded 0.5 mm tolerance. Existing documents keep their stated value.\n- **Named, non-blocking advisory:** a new `Warning::ProbeSearch` flags any probe distance past `SEARCH_LIMIT_MM` (2 mm). Like `Scallop`, it never holds the post, so old 5 mm documents still post. It is wired into the UI warning list, MCP `job` and `warned_moves`.\n- **Protected approach:** `probing::probe_cycle` now opens with a positioning rapid that ends at the **safe plane** over the first start, then **feeds** at the seek feed down to the approach point. No probe rapid runs below the safe plane. The positioning rapid is zero-length in the path's frame, because the path cannot know the tool-change position, and every post writes it as its positioning block. That keeps the Fanuc post from feeding diagonally from the tool change.\n- **Probe page hint:** it now says the distance is a search **limit**, not a destination, and that over 2 mm is flagged.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/570-probe-search-and-approach.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- **Before**, Fanuc golden: `G00 X-22 Y5 Z25` (a rapid to the approach point).\n- **After**, the same golden:\n  ```\n  G00 X-22 Y5 Z50\n  G01 X-22 Y5 Z25 F300\n  ```\n- The 770MX run with a hand-edited approach-as-feed and a Z-0.05 search touched at Z≈0. G54 Z moved from -8.3252 to -8.3259, a 0.0007 in correction, in line with a manual 0.0009 check.\n\n## How tested\n\n- **New `crates/app/tests/probe_search.rs`, 3/3:**\n  - `a_new_probe_op_searches_a_short_way_past_the_face`: the seed follows its tolerance and draws no advisory.\n  - `a_deep_search_is_named_and_never_holds_the_post`\n  - `below_the_safe_plane_a_probe_only_feeds`: Face, Edge, Corner, Bore and Boss. It **fails on the old cycle** with \"positioning ends at the safe plane, not 15\".\n- **Fixtures:** `probe_pick` and `probe_reach` move to the new 1 mm default, since they stand for new ops. `probe_op` and `fanuc_post` keep 5 mm, standing for old documents.\n- **Goldens:** the 3 Fanuc probe goldens are regenerated, with one line added each. No snapshot changed.\n- **`scripts/gate.sh quick`:** sim, motion and app suites ran 2307 passed, 0 failed. The ui suites are green except the 3 known headless-GPU tests on this host (\"No suitable graphics adapter found\"), which are environmental.\n- **Named:** probe_search 3, probe_op 11, probe_reach 5, probe_pick 9, fanuc_post 11, posting 17, conformance 6.\n- **Clippy** on app, ui, motion and sim with `-D warnings`: clean.\n- Fork synced at v0.15.0.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe post straight from this build on the real 770MX. The hand-edited equivalent ran clean, but PathPilot flagged \"Axis XY not specified\" on the hand edit, which this post's `startXY` G0 X Y avoids.\n\n**Stacked after this, by the M3:** #574 (an explicit M5 after a probe's tool change), then #575 (report the deviation).\n\nChangelog: A new probe op searches only 1 mm past the expected face (was 5 mm), a probe distance over 2 mm is flagged, and a probe never rapids below the safe plane - it feeds down to its approach point (#570)\n\nFixes #570\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
